  "content": {
    "id": "p18-problem-1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "[Proving the Quotient Rule]\n\nLet $u$ and $v$ be functions of $x$ with derivatives $u'$ and $v'$ respectively. Define the quotient $f(x)=\\frac{u}{v}$. Assume $v(x)\\ne 0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-problem-1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By expressing the quotient as $f(x)=uv^{-1}$, show that\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{u'v-v'u}{v^2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=\\frac{u'v-v'u}{v^2}$.\n\nApply the product rule to $uv^{-1}$ and the chain rule to $v^{-1}$.",
          "worked": "Apply the product rule to $uv^{-1}$ and the chain rule to $v^{-1}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} f'(x)&=u'v^{-1}+u(-v^{-2}v')\\\\ f'(x)&=\\frac{u'}{v}-\\frac{uv'}{v^2}\\\\ f'(x)&=\\frac{u'v-v'u}{v^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-problem-1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use this formula to differentiate $f(x)=\\frac{3x-1}{2x+1}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{(2x+1)^2}$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne -\\frac12$, take $u=3x-1$ and $v=2x+1$, so $u'=3$ and $v'=2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} f'(x)&=\\frac{3(2x+1)-2(3x-1)}{(2x+1)^2}\\\\ f'(x)&=\\frac{6x+3-6x+2}{(2x+1)^2}\\\\ f'(x)&=\\frac{5}{(2x+1)^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      }
    ]
  },
